module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalFunctions.StalkFormalFunctionsFrom02O8
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.CohomologyAdicDerivedComparison

/-!
# The properness clause of Tag 0A0M: the `R¹lim` term vanishes, with nothing assumed

[Stacks, Tag 0A0M] produces, for `A` Noetherian, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` with `X`
Noetherian and `ℱ` coherent with `H^p(X, ℱ)` finite over `A`, short exact sequences

`0 ⟶ R¹lim H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ H^p(X, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ lim H^p(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ 0`,

and then asserts that **if `f` is proper the `R¹lim` term is zero**. This file proves that
assertion with nothing assumed: for a proper `f` over a Noetherian base and a coherent `ℱ`,

`R¹lim H^q(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) = 0` for every `q`,

and hence `H^{q+1}(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ≅ lim H^{q+1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)`.

The chain is assembled, not built here. `Stacks.Algebraization`
`.exists_iso_cohomology_limit_adicQuotients_of_reesFinite` of
`Completion/CohomologyAdicDerivedComparison.lean` draws that conclusion from one hypothesis
`h02O8`, the Rees-finiteness of `⨁ₙ Hᵖ(X, 𝓘ⁿℱ)` of [Stacks, Tag 02O8] quantified over every
Noetherian base ring, ideal, proper scheme over it, coherent module and degree; and
`Stacks.FormalFunctions.isReesFinite_cohomologyIdealPowerSystem` of
`FormalFunctions/StalkFormalFunctionsFrom02O8.lean` is exactly that bundle, proved — it quantifies
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.isCohomologyReesFinite` ([Stacks, Tag 02O8], of
`FormalFunctions/ReesCohomologyFiniteReduction.lean`) over its data. Neither module imports the
other, so the discharge is performed here, in a leaf.

Prose in several modules of this subtree said, until this file was written, that the chain was
blocked above [Stacks, Tag 02O8] by [Stacks, Tag 0897] part (1). That is no longer so: Tag 02O8
is proved, and with it [Stacks, Tag 02OA], [Stacks, Tag 02OB] and the properness clause of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0M].

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isZero_firstDerivedLimit_cohomology_adicQuotients_of_isProper` — **the
  properness clause of [Stacks, Tag 0A0M]**: for a proper `f` the `R¹lim` term of that tag's
  sequence vanishes, in the cokernel model the sequence uses.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_iso_cohomology_limit_adicQuotients_of_isProper` — the conclusion
  the source draws from it, `H^{q+1}(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ≅ lim H^{q+1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)`.

## Why no `@[stacks 0A0M]` attribute is attached

[Stacks, Tag 0A0M] has two parts, and a tag goes only on a declaration proving all of it. The
part proved here is the properness clause. Both parts together are
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_whole` of
`Completion/GeneralCohomologyAdicCompletion.lean`, which carries the tag and which consumes
`Stacks.Algebraization.isZero_firstDerivedLimit_cohomology_adicQuotients_of_isProper_int` — this
file's result, extended from `q : ℕ` to every `q : ℤ`, the tower being identically zero in
negative degrees.

## How the other part is proved

The sequence with `H^p(X, ℱ)^∧` in the middle is
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology` transported along the
hypothesis `hBLX`, an isomorphism

`C(RΓ(X, ℱ)) ≅ RΓ(X, (lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)[0])` in `D(A)`,

`C` a reflector onto the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`. That hypothesis is discharged at
an arbitrary ideal, by `Stacks.Algebraization.hBLX_baseIdealSheaf`, as the composite of:

* the identity `RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] at an ideal sheaf generated by
  finitely many global sections of `𝒪`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`), read at
  the small Zariski site of `X` and at the ideal sheaf generated by the images `ρ a_i` of a
  generating family of `I`, which a Noetherian `A` provides;
* part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K], `ℱ^∧ = lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` with an ordinary limit
  (`Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_completion_limit_adicQuotientSystem`), read at `I · 𝒪_X`
  through `Stacks.Algebraization.baseIdealSheaf_eq_koszulIdealSheafData`; and
* `Stacks.Algebraization.derivedGlobalSectionsOverSiteIso`, which identifies the ringed-site and
  schemes-level models of `RΓ(X, -)` so that the two can be composed.

Part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] is proved directly, by the Koszul route and [Stacks, Tag 0H9L],
not via part (1) of the same tag; the identification of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E]'s tower with the
Koszul complex of `ℱ` and the comparison of `baseIdealSheaf A I f` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` are the last two bullet points above.

One route genuinely does not work, and the reason is worth keeping.
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_of_isDerivedLimit` of
`DerivedCompletionRinged/FiniteTypeIdealPending099E.lean` proves the sequence from a *natural
isomorphism* of towers `RΓ(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ≅ RΓ(X, ℱ) ⊗^𝐋_A A/Iⁿ`. Levelwise that is false at this
tag's hypotheses: take `A = k[x]`, `I = (x)`, `X = Spec A` and `ℱ` the coherent module `A/x`, for
which `H^0(X, ℱ)` is finite over `A` and the higher cohomology vanishes. Then `𝓘ⁿℱ = 0` and
`ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ = ℱ` for `n ≥ 1`, so the left hand side is `A/x` in degree zero, whereas
`(A/x) ⊗^𝐋_{k[x]} k[x]/xⁿ` has `A/x` in degree `0` and `A/x` in degree `-1`. Only a
pro-isomorphism of the two towers can hold, so that engine cannot be instantiated.

